IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-actors`

-- ccc30-forms-dna.l4 -- FORM 5.01 to FORM 5.09 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (raw text lines 17721-17909):
-- the DNA Forms: the information, warrant, orders, authorizations, summons, arrest warrant, report and applications for the taking of bodily substances.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- WHAT IS A RULE HERE. The informations, applications and the report (5.01, 5.05, 5.07, 5.08) are the officer's documents and the recitals ("Whereas ... has been
-- convicted ... a primary designated offence within the meaning of section 487.04") restate the grounds of sections 487.05 to 487.091, which another part owns:
-- all of that is prescribed wording. What is encoded is what the Forms that reach the person say beyond their wording: who may take the samples and on what conditions
-- (5.02, 5.03, 5.04, 5.06, 5.09), the order and the summons to appear, what follows if the person fails to appear (5.041 and 5.061, which quote sections 487.0551(1)
-- and 487.0552(1) in full) and the force a summons allows (5.061).
-- NAMES. The two quoted sections belong to another part, which encodes them under its own `s 487.0551(1)` and `s 487.0552(1)` names; what is encoded here is what
-- the FORM says, under `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) ...` names, so that the two parts' names can never meet (NOTES.md, Seams).
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). Every JUST FALSE branch carries a FALSE-kind comment that quotes
-- the words; every NOTHING branch carries a NOTHING-kind comment. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Forms 5.02, 5.03, 5.04, 5.06 and 5.09 -- who may take the samples`

-- Each of the five instruments authorizes the taking of "the number of samples of bodily substances that [is/are] reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis",
-- "provided that" the person taking them is able, by training or experience, to take them by the procedures of subsection 487.06(1) and "that, if the person taking the
-- samples is not a peace officer," they take them under the direction of a peace officer; and it is "subject to the following terms and conditions" (left blank in the Form:
-- the judge's own terms, a plain input here).

-- src:17756 | This is therefore to authorize and require you to take from (name of person) or cause to be taken by a person acting under your direction, the number of samples of bodily substances that are reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis, provided that the person taking the samples is able by virtue of training or experience to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code and provided that, if the person taking the samples is not a peace officer, he or she take the samples under the direction of a peace officer. This warrant is subject to the following terms and conditions that I consider advisable to ensure that the taking of the samples is reasonable in the circumstances:
@ref Form 5.02 (Subsection 487.05(1)) Warrant Authorizing the Taking of Bodily Substances for Forensic DNA Analysis, who may take the samples (src:17756)
GIVEN `the person taking the samples is able by virtue of training or experience to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person taking the samples is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person taking the samples takes them under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of samples taken is no more than the number reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any terms and conditions stated in the warrant are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.02 the warrant authorizes the person to take the samples` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person taking the samples is able by virtue of training or experience to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the person taking the samples is able by virtue of training or experience to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code"
        IF NOT (`the person taking the samples is a peace officer` OR `the person taking the samples takes them under the direction of a peace officer`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that, if the person taking the samples is not a peace officer, he or she take the samples under the direction of a peace officer"
        IF NOT `the number of samples taken is no more than the number reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the number of samples of bodily substances that are reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis"
        IF NOT `any terms and conditions stated in the warrant are complied with`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This warrant is subject to the following terms and conditions that I consider advisable"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:17766 | Therefore, you are authorized to take or cause to be taken from (name of person) the number of samples of bodily substances that is reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis, provided that the person taking the samples is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code and that, if the person taking the samples is not a peace officer, they take them under the direction of a peace officer.
