      `the person taking the samples is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person taking the samples takes them under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of samples taken is no more than the number reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any terms and conditions stated in the order are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person taking the samples is able by virtue of training or experience to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the person taking the samples is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code"
        IF NOT (`the person taking the samples is a peace officer` OR `the person taking the samples takes them under the direction of a peace officer`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and that, if the person taking the samples is not a peace officer, they take them under the direction of a peace officer"
        IF NOT `the number of samples taken is no more than the number reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the number of samples of bodily substances that is reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis"
        IF NOT `any terms and conditions stated in the order are complied with`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This order is subject to the following terms and conditions that the court considers advisable"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

