-- Forms 5.06 and 5.09 do not repeat "the number of samples ... reasonably required": they authorize "those samples" / "those additional samples", the number the application
-- asked for, so their third limb reads the number the instrument itself authorizes. The caller states whether no more than that number was taken.

§ `Form 5.041 and Form 5.061 -- the order and the summons to appear, and what follows if the person does not`

DECLARE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument` IS ONE OF
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)`
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11)`
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)`
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)`
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act`
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument`

DECLARE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 action` IS ONE OF
    `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances`

-- Form 5.041, quoting section 487.0551(1): "If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a
-- summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3), a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for their arrest in Form 5.062 to allow samples of bodily substances to be taken."
-- "a justice of the peace may issue" is a power limited by its "If": the person did appear, so the sentence is silent (NOTHING, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE). An instrument the sentence does not list (including the National Defence Act orders, which only section 487.0552(1) names): NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only").
-- src:17795 | 487.0551 (1) If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3), a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for their arrest in Form 5.062 to allow samples of bodily substances to be taken.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, quoting section 487.0551(1) (src:17795)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear at the place, day and time set out in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person failed to appear at the place, day and time set out in the instrument`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER instrument
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3)"
            WHEN `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3)"

-- Form 5.041, quoting section 487.0552(1): "Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) of this Act or
-- under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) of this Act, is guilty of (a) an indictable
-- offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- The offence is defined by a "Every person who" clause: a person outside it is not covered (NOTHING). "without reasonable excuse" limits it: a reasonable excuse is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:17797 | 487.0552 (1) Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) of this Act or under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) of this Act, is guilty of
-- src:17798 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:17799 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, quoting section 487.0552(1) (src:17797-17799)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF instrument EQUALS `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) of this Act or under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) of this Act"
        IF NOT `the person failed to comply with the instrument`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order"
        IF `the person has a reasonable excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction." Two limbs, so the class
-- is the core's "both indictable and punishable on summary conviction" and there are two Punishments. Limb (b) states no punishment (section 787, another part, fixes it): "no ... is stated".
-- src:17798 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:17799 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, quoting section 487.0552(1)(a) and (b) (src:17798-17799)
`form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the class of offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:17798 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, quoting section 487.0552(1)(a) (src:17798)
GIVETH A Punishment
`form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:17799 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, quoting section 487.0552(1)(b) (src:17799)
GIVETH A Punishment
`form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- "You are warned that failure to appear in accordance with this order may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest under subsection 487.0551(1)."
-- The warning applies to a failure to appear: a person who did appear is outside its words (NOTHING). It points at the quoted section 487.0551(1) for what may follow.
-- src:17793 | You are warned that failure to appear in accordance with this order may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest under subsection 487.0551(1) of the Criminal Code. You are also warned that failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1) of that Act.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, the warnings (src:17793)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear in accordance with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.041 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the order may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` MEANS
    IF `the person failed to appear in accordance with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "failure to appear in accordance with this order may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest"

-- "You are also warned that failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)."
-- src:17793 | You are warned that failure to appear in accordance with this order may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest under subsection 487.0551(1) of the Criminal Code. You are also warned that failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1) of that Act.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, the warnings (src:17793)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear in accordance with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.041 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person failed to appear in accordance with the order`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)"
        IF `the person has a reasonable excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "This is therefore to order you, in Her Majesty's name, to appear on (date), at (hour), at (place), for the purpose of the taking of bodily substances ...": the duty, with the days
-- until the day set out as the input.
-- src:17792 | This is therefore to order you, in Her Majesty’s name, to appear on (date), at (hour), at (place), for the purpose of the taking of bodily substances by means of the investigative procedures set out in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code.
@ref Form 5.041 (Subsections 487.051(4) and 487.055(3.11)) Order to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken, the order to appear (src:17792)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `forms 1 to 23 addressee` `forms 5.041 and 5.061 action`
`form 5.041 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` MEANS
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
    MUST `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
         BECAUSE "Form 5.041: the person did not appear as ordered (a warrant for arrest may be issued under subsection 487.0551(1); without reasonable excuse it is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1))"

-- Form 5.061 (the summons). The same two sections are quoted again: each quotation is its own text and gets its own functions, which hand the case to Form 5.041's.
-- src:17847 | 487.0551 (1) If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3), a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for their arrest in Form 5.062 to allow samples of bodily substances to be taken.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, quoting section 487.0551(1) (src:17847)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear at the place, day and time set out in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` MEANS
    `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` `the person failed to appear at the place, day and time set out in the instrument` instrument

-- src:17849 | 487.0552 (1) Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) of this Act or under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) of this Act, is guilty of
-- src:17850 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:17851 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, quoting section 487.0552(1) (src:17849-17851)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person failed to comply with the instrument` `the person has a reasonable excuse` instrument

-- src:17850 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:17851 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, quoting section 487.0552(1)(a) and (b) (src:17850-17851)
`form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the class of offence` MEANS `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the class of offence`

-- src:17850 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, quoting section 487.0552(1)(a) (src:17850)
GIVETH A Punishment
`form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`

-- src:17851 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, quoting section 487.0552(1)(b) (src:17851)
GIVETH A Punishment
`form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`

-- src:17845 | You are warned that failure to appear in accordance with this summons may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest under subsection 487.0551(1) of the Criminal Code. You are also warned that failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1) of that Act.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, the warnings (src:17845)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear in accordance with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.061 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the summons may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` MEANS
    IF `the person failed to appear in accordance with the summons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "failure to appear in accordance with this summons may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest"

-- src:17845 | You are warned that failure to appear in accordance with this summons may result in a warrant being issued for your arrest under subsection 487.0551(1) of the Criminal Code. You are also warned that failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1) of that Act.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, the warnings (src:17845)
GIVEN `the person failed to appear in accordance with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.061 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person failed to appear in accordance with the summons`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)"
        IF `the person has a reasonable excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "This is therefore to command you, in Her Majesty's name, to appear on , the day of , A.D. , at o'clock, at , for the purpose of the taking of bodily substances ...":
-- src:17844 | This is therefore to command you, in Her Majesty’s name, to appear on , the day of , A.D. , at o’clock, at , for the purpose of the taking of bodily substances by means of the investigative procedures set out in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code. A peace officer, or a person who is acting under a peace officer’s direction, who takes the samples of bodily substances may use as much force as necessary to do so.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, the command to appear (src:17844)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the summons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `forms 1 to 23 addressee` `forms 5.041 and 5.061 action`
`form 5.061 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` MEANS
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
    MUST `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the summons`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
         BECAUSE "Form 5.061: the person did not appear as summoned (a warrant for arrest may be issued under subsection 487.0551(1); without reasonable excuse it is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1))"

-- "A peace officer, or a person who is acting under a peace officer's direction, who takes the samples of bodily substances may use as much force as necessary to do so."
-- A grant limited by its own wording: to whom (a peace officer or a person acting under their direction), for what (taking the samples) and how much (as much as necessary).
-- A case outside any of the three limits is not covered (NOTHING); the text does not say "may not".
-- src:17844 | This is therefore to command you, in Her Majesty’s name, to appear on , the day of , A.D. , at o’clock, at , for the purpose of the taking of bodily substances by means of the investigative procedures set out in subsection 487.06(1) of the Criminal Code. A peace officer, or a person who is acting under a peace officer’s direction, who takes the samples of bodily substances may use as much force as necessary to do so.
@ref Form 5.061 (Subsections 487.055(4) and 487.091(3)) Summons to a Person To Have Bodily Substances Taken for Forensic DNA Analysis, the force that may be used (src:17844)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer or is acting under a peace officer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes the samples of bodily substances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force used is no more than is necessary to take the samples` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.061 the person may use the force used` MEANS
    IF `the person is a peace officer or is acting under a peace officer's direction`
       AND `the person takes the samples of bodily substances`
       AND `the force used is no more than is necessary to take the samples`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer, or a person who is acting under a peace officer’s direction, who takes the samples of bodily substances may use as much force as necessary to do so"
